  "title": "Turtles play an important role in the world’s oceans and marine food ...",
  "description": "Turtles play an important role in the world’s oceans and marine food chains. Some species feed on jellyfish, controlling their populations. Others feed on seagrass beds that stimulate their growth which provide nursery habitat for fish stocks, making them important for fisheries and ultimately food security. Healthy seagrass can also help to clean a sea's waters and reduce coastal erosion. But Malaysia's turtles are slowly facing extinction. Already endangered, they face a new threat in rising temperatures caused by climate change, which is disrupting the balance of male and female baby turtles that hatch from nests. Universiti Malaysia Terengganu noted that the number of male turtles hatched from 2019 to 2022 on many areas on Peninsular Malaysia's East Coast is almost zero (Al-Jazeera, April 2024). Turtle eggs laid incubate for as long as 60 days in the sand and are extremely sensitive to temperature. At 29.2 degrees Celsius (84.6 Fahrenheit), a green turtle nest will result in an equal share of males and females. A single degree in temperature change can completely shift the overall gender of a nest in one or another direction. A big thanks to Universiti Malaysia Terengganu's Sea Turtle Unit, who have provided the footage of the turtle hatchlings and green turtle underwater shots, and who were absolutely stellar when hosting me at the Chagar Hutang Turtle Sanctuary. All other footage done by me. If you want to volunteer to help save Malaysia's turtles or just want to be aware of them, check out the Sea Turtle Unit (SeaTRU) today! Did you know that turtle and marine conservation is covered under the UN's Sustainable Development Goals (SDG)? For more info on this, check out SDG14. MUSIC: Musictown - Pensive Mood Guitar and Cello, from Pixabay ARTISTE: https://pixabay.com/users/musictown-25873992/ LINK: https://pixabay.com/music/ambient-pensive-mood-guitar-and-cello-21666/ #turtles #turtlesmalaysia #penyu #penyumalaysia #climatechange #climate #sdg14 #sustainabledevelopmentgoals #critical2 ",
